/**
 * Vercel Web Analytics — anonymous page-view + visitor tracking for
 * the marketing site (`kiln3d.com`).
 *
 * Why we use it:
 *   * Answers "is the marketing site getting traffic, where do
 *     visitors land, what's the bounce rate" — the shape of data
 *     we need before turning on paid acquisition.
 *   * First-party-feeling — Vercel is already our hosting subprocessor,
 *     and Web Analytics is operated by the same vendor with the same
 *     SCC posture (see PRIVACY.md §5).
 *   * No cookies, no PII, no cross-site tracking.  IP address is
 *     hashed with a daily-rotating salt before storage, then
 *     discarded — visitor counts are de-duplicated within a UTC day
 *     but not across days, by design.
 *   * No GDPR consent banner required (because no cookies and no
 *     persistent identifiers).
 *
 * Why we use it ONLY on the marketing site:
 *   * The web workshop (`app.kiln3d.com`) already has every
 *     authenticated event covered via its own signed-in telemetry —
 *     adding Vercel Analytics there would be redundant data
 *     surface for zero new signal.
 *   * The marketing site is anonymous-by-design and the only place
 *     we genuinely don't know what's happening today.
 *
 * Implementation:
 *   * Static deferred-script include of Vercel's hosted script.
 *     Vercel auto-injects the project context server-side at the
 *     platform level, so no env var or project ID is required.
 *   * On non-Vercel deployments (local dev preview at :4321,
 *     custom hosts) the request to `/_vercel/insights/script.js`
 *     404s harmlessly — the page still renders, just without
 *     analytics.
 *   * No <noscript> fallback — analytics that requires JavaScript
 *     is fine for our purposes; no-JS visitors don't show up in
 *     the dashboard, which we accept as a small undercount.
 *
 * Disclosure:
 *   * Documented in PRIVACY.md §3.2 (analytics) and §5 (subprocessor
 *     table — Vercel's scope expanded to include Web Analytics).
 *
 * Disable for development:
 *   * The script does nothing on `localhost` because Vercel's
 *     edge layer doesn't serve `_vercel/insights/script.js` from
 *     local Astro dev.  No flag needed.
 */
---

<!-- Vercel Web Analytics — see /src/components/VercelAnalytics.astro -->
<script defer src="/_vercel/insights/script.js"></script>
